% ====================================================
% REPEAT — Isaiah 40:1–8
% Source: black ink, photo 34 (PXL_20261105_235736930.jpg)
% Compare with: Isaiah/40.tex (blue ink, photos 33 and 35)
% ====================================================
  \pa \verse{40:1} ``Greatly comfort My people,''%
  \lit{comfort ye, comfort ye\ldots}%
  \ed{\textit{piel} imperative}
  \pa says your God.%%

  \pa \verse{40:2} ``Speak to the heart of Jerusalem;%
  \ed{wot?}%
  \ed{go to the hearts of the people in Jerusalem}
  \pa call to her%%

  \pb that her warfare\alt{service, hard labor} is completed,\pa that her punishment has been accepted,\alt{paid for,}%%

  \pb that she's received from the \lord's hand\pa double for all her sins.%%

  \pb \verse{40:3} The voice crying%%

  \pc in the wilderness: prepare\pa the way of the \lord.%%

  \pc Make straight in the desert\pa a highway to our God.%%

  \pb \verse{40:4} Every valley shall be lifted up\pa and every mountain and hill shall be brought low.%%

  \pc The crooked shall become straight,\pa the rough places a plain.%%

  \pb \verse{40:5} The glory of the \lord\ shall be revealed;\pa all flesh shall see it together,%%

  \pa for the mouth of the \lord\ has \understood{so} spoken.''%%

  \pa \verse{40:6} A voice says, ``Cry!''\pa And he says,\alt{replies,} ``What shall I cry?''%%

  \pb ``All flesh is grass.\pa All its goodliness\alt{comeliness} is as a flower of the field.%%

  \pa \verse{40:7} The grass shall wither, the flower shall fade\pa because the spirit of the \lord\ will blow upon it.\pa Surely the people are grass.%
  \ed{God is so much greater than we are, no matter how tough we think we are.}%%

  \pa \verse{40:8} The grass shall wither, the flower shall fade,\pa but the word of our God shall stand forever.''%%

